{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7050437","formula":"C₃₃H₂₅N₃O₃","hill":"C33H25N3O3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":33.0,"H":25.0,"N":3.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"Norbormide"},"descriptions":{"en":"Norbormide (Raticate, Shoxin) is a toxic compound used as a rodenticide. It has several mechanisms of action, acting as a vasoconstrictor and calcium channel blocker, but is selectively toxic to rats and has relatively low toxicity to other species, due to a species specific action of opening the permeability transition pores in rat mitochondria. It is classified as an extremely hazardous substance in the United States as defined in Section 302 of the U.S. Emergency Planning and Community Right-to-Know Act (42 U.S.C. 11002), and is subject to strict reporting requirements by facilities which produce, store, or use it in significant quantities."},"fame":7,"pubchemCid":13814,"mass":511.6,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC=C(C=C1)C(=C2C3C=C(C2C4C3C(=O)NC4=O)C(C5=CC=CC=C5)(C6=CC=CC=N6)O)C7=CC=CC=N7","inchikey":"DNTHHIVFNQZZRD-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"8-(hydroxy-phenyl-pyridin-2-ylmethyl)-10-[phenyl(pyridin-2-yl)methylidene]-4-azatricyclo[5.2.1.02,6]dec-8-ene-3,5-dione","classes":[{"qid":"Q59199015","names":{"en":"group of stereoisomers","ru":"группа стереоизомеров","uk":"група стереоізомерів"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"13814","atoms":64,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":3.097,"y":3.818,"z":0.265,"el":"C"},{"x":2.312,"y":3.141,"z":1.197,"el":"C"},{"x":1.991,"y":1.798,"z":0.995,"el":"C"},{"x":2.454,"y":1.123,"z":-0.142,"el":"C"},{"x":3.244,"y":1.809,"z":-1.072,"el":"C"},{"x":3.563,"y":3.153,"z":-0.869,"el":"C"},{"x":2.124,"y":-0.302,"z":-0.362,"el":"C"},{"x":0.871,"y":-0.598,"z":-0.762,"el":"C"},{"x":0.163,"y":-1.91,"z":-1.029,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.096,"y":-1.699,"z":-0.202,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.397,"y":-0.38,"z":-0.246,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.314,"y":0.287,"z":-1.092,"el":"